      "text": "The first discount of $20\\%$ reduces the price to $30 - 0.20(30) = 30 - 6$ dollars or $24$ dollars. \nThen the second discount of $25\\%$ reduces the price to $24 - 0.25(24) = 24 - 6$ dollars or $18$ dollars. \nTo find the single percent discount, we need to find the discount that reduces the price from $30$ to $18$. \nThe amount of money saved is $\\$30 - \\$18 = \\$12$. \nTo find the single percent discount, we divide the amount of money saved by the original price: \n$\\frac{\\$12}{\\$30} = \\frac{2}{5} = 0.40$. \nTo convert this decimal to a percent, we multiply by $100$: \n$0.40 \\times 100 = \\boxed{40\\%}$. \nThe answer is: 40",
